#
# Why this run: data/evidence/emission_decision.json is the pre-registered rule "change the default
# shaping only if a candidate beats the shipped policy by > 0.01 on the new-fault-like population
# AND reproduces on a second, independently trained ensemble".  The first ensemble's extended sweep
# (run 35262778745, 152 candidates) put the best hard candidate at floor 0.1 with width 0 px
# (0.136452 against the shipped policy's 0.041041 on the same field), with widening HURTING at that
# floor - so the candidate to reproduce is a floor change, and the labelling below is what lets
# scripts/decide_emission_width.py consume this sweep as the second ensemble (`--second-sweep`).
#
# RUN_ID is ensemble 2 (folds 6-11, seed 43, branch arena/01a0b043-gemsdoe).  Four of its six folds
# carry artifacts (fold 4 died in training, fold 3 is a straggler still training); the sweep takes
# whatever `fold-*` artifacts the run exposes, so it blends 4 live folds here and would blend 5 if
# it were re-fired after fold 3 lands.
#
# The grid is kept IDENTICAL to the first ensemble's sweep on purpose: the reproduction compares
# like with like (same floors, same widths, same ramp candidates) and the contrast is taken per
# floor inside each sweep, never across sweeps.
